<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Common Prayer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1549</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of Common Prayer is the prayer book of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a>, first issued in 1549 under Edward VI and largely composed by Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-cranmer">Thomas Cranmer</a>. It replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> services with a single English liturgy, revised in 1552, 1559 and 1662. The 1662 version remained the official liturgy for centuries, and its language and forms spread throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglicanism">Anglican Communion</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-common-prayer.jpg" alt="Book of Common Prayer" width="320" height="549" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Church of England · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Book_of_Common_Prayer_1760.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
